WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:11.690
E. Lockhart &amp; Maureen Johnson: Good morning
Hank!

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:17.609
John: Those are world-famous writers Maureen
Johnson and E. Lockhart. By the way, the Brotherhood

00:00:17.609 --> 00:00:18.970
2 website looks awesome.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:22.310
It's 6:30 in the morning, I am extremely tired,
and I have a long day of writing ahead of

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:28.810
me. So we're gonna make this quick, and we're
gonna do it school style.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:34.480
First period: Math. I would like to briefly
explain the 70/42 mishap. What happened was

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.820
that I incorrectly believed, and indeed have
always believed, that each minute contains

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:47.320
100 seconds. Were that to be true, there would
be 70 5-second segments in each 3 minute and

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.360
30 second period.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.910
It turns out, and this is extraordinarily
difficult news for me to accept, that each

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:59.850
minute only contains sixty seconds, and therefore
there's only 42 5-second segments in each

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:04.470
3 minute and 30 second period. This is a tragedy
not only for the American minute, but also

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:08.860
for me personally. It makes the fact that
the first draft of my new novel is due in

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:13.500
8,640 minutes 40 percent more terrifying.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.939
Second period: It's supposed to be history,
but your teacher is lazy and all you ever

00:01:16.939 --> 00:01:21.070
do is watch TV shows he taped. Hank, I feel
like one of my duties to you, as the brother

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:26.450
who does own a working television, is to keep
you informed periodically about what's going

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:30.990
on in the world of entertainment. Paula Abdul
has a drug problem. Ivanka Trump is improbably

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:31.990
attractive.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:36.130
Period Three: Physical Education. Hank, the
Bears are just one game away from the Superbowl,

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:41.400
and if I have my way, I will be filming Brotherhood
2.0 from the Superbowl.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.540
Fourth Period: English. Hank, your Battle
of the Books inspired me to have my own Battle

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:48.770
of the Books because I thought that your Battle
of the Books was hilarious, and then I thought

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:51.950
maybe my Battle of the Books could be kind
of like a pale imitation, and people would

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:56.420
laugh and say "well, it's good, but it's not
as funny as Hank's" and you know, that's pretty

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:57.899
much my goal with this thing.

00:01:57.899 --> 00:02:01.950
Round one: The American edition of Looking
for Alaska versus the Dutch edition of Looking

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.090
for Alaska.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:06.340
(American): Hey, how's it goin?

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:07.409
(Dutch): OK, how are you?

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:09.509
(American): Hey, why don't you have an accent?

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:12.430
(Dutch): Uh, I don't, I don't do accents,
I think they're weird.

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:15.230
(American): AAAHHHRRRAAARAARAA (pants)

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:26.260
(in high voice): Oh wait, no! It's the Danish
edition of Looking for Alaska! Dodadoodadoodadooo!

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:30.530
And the British edition! Wait are the British
on the American sides? Or are they on the

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:37.530
Dutch sides? Oh my God, they're for Europe,
not America!

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:44.980
It wasn't until I started editing that that
I realized: Oh my God, I am such a loser.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:48.850
I can't even bring myself to show you the
Hemingway versus Faulkner one, it's even more

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:49.850
embarrassing.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:53.430
Announcements: Hank, could you possibly mail
me some of the misprinted EcoGeek business

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:57.489
cards, just like, five of them? Thanks. You
can get my address from Mom and Dad. Also,

00:02:57.489 --> 00:03:04.080
can we agree to have our Happy Dance compilation
video done around the end of February?

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:09.560
Okay, okay, okay. Big day, big day, big day,
big day. 2,000 words, 2,000 words, 2,000 words,

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.450
2,000 words. Okay, I'm gonna go back to bed.

